+### Dev/SRE Toolbox (`/api/toolbox`) — requires Basic Auth
+Modular, local, bounded and synchronous technical utilities inside the existing app.
+No network call, no Kubernetes cluster, no external credential, no queue, no
+persistence. See [docs/14-dev-sre-toolbox.md](docs/14-dev-sre-toolbox.md) for the full
+reference, limits and limitations.
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| GET | `/api/toolbox/tools` | Catalogue: id, description, version and input schema of every tool |
+| POST | `/api/toolbox/runs` | Run one tool and return a uniform typed result with a `run_id` |
+
+Tools: `json.validate`, `text.diff`, `k8s.manifest.inspect`.
+
+bash
+# List the tools
+curl -s -u admin:password http://localhost:8000/api/toolbox/tools | python3 -m json.tool
+
+# Validate a JSON document
+curl -s -u admin:password -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/toolbox/runs \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"tool": "json.validate", "input": {"text": "{\"a\": 1}"}}' | python3 -m json.tool
+
+
 ### MCP Server (`/api/mcp`) — requires Basic Auth
